 normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-3,-7,-8⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027279ba-c86b-5b53-9b4f-d91a6c95b4d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336052} {:answer/id #uuid "2b335037-3eda-5eb1-a665-40e27aacca2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336439} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc9ad4f-0956-53af-9375-a4dc1247e499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336605} {:answer/id #uuid "924674c9-4ac4-5fac-bce9-febfcdbeeeee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337359} {:answer/id #uuid "faf5ff12-8cff-5606-9806-8c51dfe352b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336439} :answer-field/id #uuid "0006422d-58d9-51c7-8d8f-f4fd7450f036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b2e1c378-a183-516b-92fd-1753dcbc375f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70972" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $w=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,1⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13372795-1d9c-59ee-ba7f-59bbde3f9d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336213} {:answer/id #uuid "14870064-b7e8-54d0-99ca-4b64bfe2bd62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336226} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7f5521-fd3a-51c7-9ecf-a3af94ee1454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336454} {:answer/id #uuid "6249715c-fc3f-56fb-9993-32d1a515b62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336915} {:answer/id #uuid "c671655c-abd1-563c-aef5-4ee4cece1841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337791} :answer-field/id #uuid "be9468de-a381-56af-b583-e970a0ac913c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3cd142bb-0e37-5169-9871-c05d6282caa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70974" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 12 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,0,4⟩$ and $w=⟨1,-1,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4i+j-3k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨4,1,-3⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e02ac0-3e89-5c73-aee7-9f2de3148d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} {:answer/id #uuid "8ffc566d-8d4c-53c3-af4b-b2d7a4d35946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391685} {:answer/id #uuid "efc39529-4f0f-5e00-b796-0c632007c03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391686} {:answer/id #uuid "f83846d5-42d7-540e-ad5c-05350b13e9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391687} {:answer/id #uuid "0693f405-c3d1-5022-a785-4b3d44119374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aebbae6-4b97-5e3f-9a17-15682100023d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3b07ac22-3309-5bc0-ac4b-6e1be0e5a45e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33823" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,2,2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3315c99a-bf65-5d24-a5cd-d108af0b9169" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,3,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410868} {:answer/id #uuid "49c23de5-10ac-588e-b906-2f601c3ee4cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410870} {:answer/id #uuid "58daaedf-85bc-5389-a9f1-135d9cf2dc54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,6,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410872} {:answer/id #uuid "68dd536e-0595-5b7f-bbf4-086bbda96dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410875} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d316ee-8c43-5cbe-ae4e-5f0454d179ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410888}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410870} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d97d655-a539-5ca4-b364-2c12300cff27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4fcca2b7-695c-58b7-b034-c1fa748f47da" :question/math-academy-id "q-128496" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,-5,1⟩+s⟨3,-6,0⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-5,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-6,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =6i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨6,3,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,3,3⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20671737-03a7-5430-89bf-040b752377e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,3,31⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429805} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5b071d-27ac-57b7-af6d-728934e76426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,5,31⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429808} {:answer/id #uuid "745f1be0-1559-5f77-9632-8cdde3498554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,31⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429809} {:answer/id #uuid "cb172289-6398-5303-bbd8-83b5e2e9bc68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,7,31⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429811} {:answer/id #uuid "dea73573-73e0-539b-8d97-0a1d8ac2f0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,27⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429812}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429809} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b496fd-8c3a-561b-bf53-11d88d290ff5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c3b23dc-4bcb-57b2-b0fc-dd67734d3e36" :question/math-academy-id "q-128493" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-7,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,5,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5i+3j+31k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,31⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,31⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426d2f86-6e44-5b72-8222-a1d8c826de45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,-5,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489666} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee143c1-2d22-5a6b-8226-53337f0c9aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489742} {:answer/id #uuid "81af70fa-ea19-54cc-83e0-b0a21fab95e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-34,-22,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489809} {:answer/id #uuid "87ba8eac-d335-511b-94ef-29242597cc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489824} {:answer/id #uuid "a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,22,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf0e22c-7173-584a-ae1b-a7c0bd01e586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70975" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨0,8,-1⟩+t⟨-1,1,7⟩+s⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,7⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-5,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =36i+22j+2k \\\\  & =⟨36,22,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨36,22,2⟩.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"} :step/id #uuid "aa340a23-a5f7-53c0-a279-cfaa2cb34f68" :step/math-academy-id 421996 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120900}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120900 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119648 :question/id #uuid "297bda8f-6e33-5cc2-a2e1-5ab6186fa9d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4941" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(2,50,-19)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 2,\\sqrt{6},17 \\rangle + s \\langle -1,7,2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 20,-44, 27 \\rangle + t \\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd010f61-f497-566f-ac0f-c50c695f2870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390876} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fe09e5-ac83-5e62-97ff-7cc91f6b67c5" :answer/