 \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨3,7,6⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,9,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨7,-2,3⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03170ce6-1b74-5d0c-a740-266903fa4105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,4,2⟩+t⟨4,-4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259902} {:answer/id #uuid "31b47527-c857-57e6-abe0-41faa15df975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨4,2,6⟩+t⟨-4,-3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260322} {:answer/id #uuid "3648beed-e103-5bec-8bc9-7ee681a02fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} {:answer/id #uuid "7a29aab3-eefc-5ee1-beae-88249bb83af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260941} {:answer/id #uuid "a7218829-3284-55b3-b600-8e4433336662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,2,4⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} :answer-field/id #uuid "0824088c-267c-5eb4-919f-03962a76134c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e20b81af-d8f6-5935-a0ab-531fc6f636f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128760" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a9595c5-d8f6-5617-b156-92b53851b716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260250} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce9642e-12a2-5cdf-b2c6-8d924f99cc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨2,\\sqrt{5},-3⟩+t⟨4,-2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260672} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdf40e-542c-5dc2-a6fd-921cd50285d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-4,2,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260838} {:answer/id #uuid "98f54aca-662b-5760-8538-8039f017575f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨-3,\\sqrt{5},2⟩+t⟨-4,2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261201} {:answer/id #uuid "c5482cde-9561-5647-92a3-a41687e26ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-5,4,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261615}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260250} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d78a6d-4a26-5561-9d61-b00f371bc511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4a48e326-aaaf-5e46-9d89-fb7681e96383" :question/math-academy-id "q-128761" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(7,-3,4)$ and $Q(5,1,-1),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,1,-1⟩-⟨7,-3,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨7,-3,4⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336bb496-d1df-5e9a-a07a-1ec951355ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302774} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8dad69-2acf-5472-9a3f-505a95ac3fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "b208b020-2e95-5012-90d1-880d0704ce1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303557} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a6125d-748b-50ac-93e6-06be995d0638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303769} {:answer/id #uuid "feb8b07e-b16f-57b2-afdf-a8e6076cfea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308e92-1035-59ed-9244-1f44706e0efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "133e1de3-de48-5298-8948-a57726f1d155" :question/math-academy-id "q-33160" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49c5cfba-30b4-5cd2-bb7b-b9327c517321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨2,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336716} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa30567-9f99-5396-b1b9-f442d2fcaa29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨1,-7,-2⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336976} {:answer/id #uuid "81128713-0ba6-54d5-ad60-664ede84fab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337202} {:answer/id #uuid "8afb07a6-2bd8-5edb-9ec6-22d1e7d02591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337287} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e1912b-7b80-5650-8872-08ddd53cd44c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337202} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6c2ae9-bf70-5d0f-96e8-5aee0a9622bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2d249e59-e724-5332-83de-2d46399e2dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-71034" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $L(-1,-1,1),\\,M(2,5,-3)$, and $N(0,-8,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =⟨2,5,-3⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =⟨0,-8,-1⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $l=⟨-1,-1,1⟩$ of the point $l,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =l+s\\overset{\\to }{LM}+t\\overset{\\to }{LN} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2337c867-1b68-51ab-bed8-d899af940e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336359} {:answer/id #uuid "337484e0-5b6b-5f95-88dc-ef0b3096b39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨3,4,-3⟩+t⟨2,0,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336518} {:answer/id #uuid "38e231b3-4c0e-5717-a0ef-ef6534f1c274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨2,0,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336565} {:answer/id #uuid "4401b429-e065-55ec-a1ab-6464c74d2d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336670} {:answer/id #uuid "f760a7c7-7e6e-53d4-8222-5b484099a2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨3,4,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338201}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336670} :answer-field/id #uuid "489447af-58f8-5125-a63d-1b42d95b0549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "238f448c-c904-543b-b4aa-7c48d6e1e778" :question/math-academy-id "q-71038" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(2,-1,0),\\,V(3,4,-3)$, and $W(2,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{UW},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨3,4,-3⟩-⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨2,0,0⟩-⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨2,-1,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abe04ef1-0077-539a-b85c-52caa98344a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366207} {:answer/id #uuid "4a96f288-3fd0-537b-806e-046844764150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366208} {:answer/id #uuid "fac45cd4-59c7-516c-bd74-1e4a54e263c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,4⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366209} {:answer/id #uuid "4e15b755-6aa5-59e8-8ede-166d794590c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366210} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4ca503-3a78-5aa5-ac98-b7e77b80a651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366211}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366211} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b9dde6c-05bb-5b0d-9060-015e400fc047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "340957e8-d465-5c3d-b1df-5f238a4c6329" :question/math-academy-id "q-71040" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $C(1,1,1)$ and $D(-3,2,4)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨0,1,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨0,1,1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =⟨-3,2,4⟩-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $c=⟨1,1,1⟩$ of the point $C,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5688ffe4-a344-59de-904d-69d4ee154888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387959} {:answer/id #uuid "f1894930-5724-5ec7-9314-304ee3857bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨1,-2,-1⟩+t⟨5,3,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387960} {:answer/id #uuid "36f474e9-d65e-5772-a687-55109749a47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,-2⟩+t⟨3,5,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387961} {:answer/id #uuid "cb27fd48-3d2d-5982-947b-b3e559f28c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,1,2⟩+t⟨-3,1,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387962} {:answer/id #uuid "17405e35-9e5b-5d7e-a665-511b494914e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387963} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b619d06-46ec-54c2-b23b-cc9a1e50c422" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d8ae8a52-91d4-5f03-bbaf-4e5a85108c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-128741" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(1,-2,3),\\,Q(3,-4,2),$ and $R(4,3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-4,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨4,3,2⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨1,-2,3⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨1,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,-1⟩+t⟨3,5,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c5c0f5-cea3-5255-8903-d2285b902635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387966} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5a335a-8c39-5296-9221-80718d983791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387967} {:answer/id #uuid "a1feedd1-adb2-5c03-b2da-3a56801de734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,0⟩+t⟨2,-3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387968} {:answer/id #uuid "9a555223-84bf-5c63-a527-b176aedbb599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨-1,3,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387969} {:answer/id #uuid "0604c24b-d46b-5997-bc46-46a6a514d076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,-1,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387966} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0f3ed1e-aca6-5323-9130-d1a84b4303b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0a7f0779-a02e-54b4-a490-a401988e7022" :question/math-academy-id "q-128745" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(3,2,-1),\\,E(3,1,-2),$ and $F(5,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨5,1,2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11fe6c60-77f7-596d-b73e-0a2b1a46b507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨2,-9,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393066} {:answer/id #uuid "18c27f61-10ac-5e9a-9262-ba682e6d266e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393067} {:answer/id #uuid "a673c983-c8f1-5b15-8abb-116913587299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} {:answer/id #uuid "f377602b-aa7b-52c3-8d62-a25cd478c050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨0,-6,-1⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393069} {:answer/id #uuid "37a16cbe-c7b9-5d98-99c1-895ad8adbfef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨2,-9,0⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} :answer-field/id #uuid "141932d6-a6f5-58b4-ba12-7fe47a40ab43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "901f1360-df93-5e5e-ac60-c5607de4f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-71036" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(3,6,2),\\,Q(2,-9,0)$, and $R(3,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,-9,0⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-15,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨3,6,2⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28f06646-216c-5c67-9be6-f9c0e54523f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-3,-2,0⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410867} {:answer/id #uuid "56c396c7-54c7-56b3-83a2-5e6b3f8f1725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410871} {:answer/id #uuid "8e59d870-815b-50b7-be77-2034640ef7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410882} {:answer/id #uuid "918bb145-9b81-5373-9e09-80bc4d524835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨-3,-2,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410883} {:answer/id #uuid "c9066316-4e88-5b51-afd6-db0ca189a8ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410890}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410871} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffaa26fc-cae0-5499-800c-9dd489ee2f5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59e1275b-72d1-5efa-8072-c2d963838f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71049" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(-3,-2,0)$ and $V(1,0,-1)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨1,0,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨-3,-2,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,-2,0⟩+s⟨-1,5,-1⟩+t⟨4,2,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076c0841-49e0-5efa-932b-cea12451f354" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429935} {:answer/id #uuid "36f17219-1319-57b9-b736-3daca3fe9f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-2,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429936} {:answer/id #uuid "42182090-ca90-5aff-919b-f97f28d17f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-3,-2,7⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429937} {:answer/id #uuid "a639639c-9709-5ea4-b9d7-eed8e4f97ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429938} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4f3967-0094-5670-b34b-c4d617495978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,4,3⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429939}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429937} :answer-field/id #uuid "918bca49-2085-5b3c-9bbd-1ed60948277f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e59ecbbf-3ac2-51fb-8da8-83763d787a9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-71033" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(1,0,-2),\\,E(-2,-2,5)$, and $F(-2,4,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨-2,-2,5⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-2,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨-2,4,3⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨1,0,-2⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-3,-2,7⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"} :step/id #uuid "a2d3f79a-dc28-5d90-9d1f-404334ec9529" :step/math-academy-id 422003}] :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120017} {:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423364} :activity/id #uuid "3089dbbe-cc2f-5f60-8b4c-786b3272c8cf" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050308} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423364 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd010f61-f497-566f-ac0f-c50c695f2870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390876} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fe09e5-ac83-5e62-97ff-7cc91f6b67c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨0,6,2⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩+t⟨6,-5,10⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390877} {:answer/id #uuid "5b991d71-53b1-55cf-8e90-ebe111f71f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨5,-3,1⟩+s⟨8,1,0⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390878} {:answer/id #uuid "c86fee90-6ade-5c0b-9714-4278894c742b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨5,-3,1⟩+s⟨8,1,0⟩+t⟨6,-5,10⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390879} {:answer/id #uuid "db01346f-8d56-5827-aa82-3725170f51a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨5,-3,1⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390880}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390880} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf886e4d-3534-5b42-92f4-88d2e9d1dbe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0602f3f6-acc2-53ef-a72e-b71caa5d5289" :question/math-academy-id "q-33066" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(5,-3,1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨8,1,0⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩$ and $r=⟨6,-5,10⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨3,2,5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,6,2⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(5,-3,1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨5,-3,1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨5,-3,1⟩+s⟨3,2,5⟩+t⟨0,6,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2f9f2ed5-353f-52bf-a2a3-853d4a9582d6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423365}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423365 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "027279ba-c86b-5b53-9b4f-d91a6c95b4d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336052} {:answer/id #uuid "2b335037-3eda-5eb1-a665-40e27aacca2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336439} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc9ad4f-0956-53af-9375-a4dc1247e499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-5,3,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336605} {:answer/id #uuid "924674c9-4ac4-5fac-bce9-febfcdbeeeee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨7,-3,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337359} {:answer/id #uuid "faf5ff12-8cff-5606-9806-8c51dfe352b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336439} :answer-field/id #uuid "0006422d-58d9-51c7-8d8f-f4fd7450f036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b2e1c378-a183-516b-92fd-1753dcbc375f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70972" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $w=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-5i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,1⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "43654397-35b1-5e26-a4f3-f83c5d045414" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423366}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423366 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7586c1e4-84f3-5128-898b-c5e464276c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,2,1⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337090} {:answer/id #uuid "82d1d2de-9e64-5f24-9d44-872a4f4b17ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨4,-1,5⟩+s⟨6,2,1⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337221} {:answer/id #uuid "85ed694c-09f9-5528-8f94-aa3dcea698e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨0,2,3⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩+t⟨6,2,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337243} {:answer/id #uuid "9294f976-ff7c-58c2-93a2-681c99675cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337366} {:answer/id #uuid "d0355145-d653-5b7e-b879-a79de4840c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,2,1⟩+s⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,9⟩+t⟨3,10,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337090} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb6f8717-8af1-5d47-bcaf-6f6357145f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "63af645f-746e-5e92-b7a0-0217edd376c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70977" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $D(6,2,1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,9⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and $r=⟨\\sqrt{3},10,-1⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $D(6,2,1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $d=⟨6,2,1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨6,2,1⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f22fda97-7410-513e-bdd3-694b01fc4928"}] :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423363} {:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429946} :activity/id #uuid "f1f3e620-4475-5a3a-a265-6ab29906aca2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050308} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429942 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840901d2-388a-56b4-b2ed-4aa835792fb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393059} {:answer/id #uuid "3a999e63-69bc-5b5b-ba4a-b3d5b35bdaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} {:answer/id #uuid "a9567360-7eeb-5790-a68a-54789a38c8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393061} {:answer/id #uuid "0abc7499-ef02-5049-b4d5-92446ade1dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,20⟩+t⟨0,3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393062} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ba868-cc5e-5eb8-8190-756b44636c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} :answer-field/id #uuid "74bd7e12-82f3-5b83-88f9-1acb2c12ad74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1e3ae2d-0bf0-5679-8209-36898e366f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70981" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6962e54d-afff-5346-b8ad-2f0747169762" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429943}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429943 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076c0841-49e0-5efa-932b-cea12451f354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429935} {:answer/id #uuid "36f17219-1319-57b9-b736-3daca3fe9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-2,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429936} {:answer/id #uuid "42182090-ca90-5aff-919b-f97f28d17f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-3,-2,7⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429937} {:answer/id #uuid "a639639c-9709-5ea4-b9d7-eed8e4f97ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429938} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4f3967-0094-5670-b34b-c4d617495978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,4,3⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429939}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429937} :answer-field/id #uuid "918bca49-2085-5b3c-9bbd-1ed60948277f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e59ecbbf-3ac2-51fb-8da8-83763d787a9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-71033" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(1,0,-2),\\,E(-2,-2,5)$, and $F(-2,4,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨-2,-2,5⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-2,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨-2,4,3⟩-⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨1,0,-2⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-3,-2,7⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "80c6a6f7-a534-55d9-a6a9-83c73859670a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429944}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429944 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4a3c41-2d3e-5406-a2cd-cbab49cb529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,-26⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260257} {:answer/id #uuid "63d710f5-99cb-53b4-8290-6299023ee722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨8,-2,17⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260737} {:answer/id #uuid "95c11743-7580-55cc-a7f1-587f795b6ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ed729-7d24-5fef-a919-3b87d20a7b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-8,2,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261244} {:answer/id #uuid "da606c57-af3e-52fa-9552-99fdba561ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-2,-8,-7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} :answer-field/id #uuid "e859b94c-82b3-57fc-b159-f1a0791b5216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "58d7da64-39e5-5263-82e1-d46d43bc9c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128497" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "87cee5fb-f33c-5202-a9b9-1f5b449bede4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429945}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429945 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "259294bf-42a6-5b1f-a914-2eeba4786e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,12,-7⟩+s⟨1,3,-5⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260203} {:answer/id #uuid "3660d937-cc87-5a73-a31f-13375df8d401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260360} {:answer/id #uuid "586437d1-d3c1-5c04-82a5-9e97897d0755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨-3,4,2⟩+t⟨1,5,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260630} {:answer/id #uuid "5a80a400-edf2-5ed4-95ef-bc093dec6a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260648} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a3a0fb-37c8-5001-bfec-42aa7883b3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261347}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260360} :answer-field/id #uuid "991622fb-4bb5-597a-a633-df7720b54e4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "75465043-c7d7-54b7-b914-8b78a961bb97" :question/math-academy-id "q-128536" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,2,4⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-22,17,13⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,5,6⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-7,12,-3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a96d0f38-f22e-54d6-9800-3b945209e167"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429946 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e02ac0-3e89-5c73-aee7-9f2de3148d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} {:answer/id #uuid "8ffc566d-8d4c-53c3-af4b-b2d7a4d35946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391685} {:answer/id #uuid "efc39529-4f0f-5e00-b796-0c632007c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391686} {:answer/id #uuid "f83846d5-42d7-540e-ad5c-05350b13e9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391687} {:answer/id #uuid "0693f405-c3d1-5022-a785-4b3d44119374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aebbae6-4b97-5e3f-9a17-15682100023d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3b07ac22-3309-5bc0-ac4b-6e1be0e5a45e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33823" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,2,2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "b87c320e-e438-5e5e-b4bc-c722b9da8264" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429942}}] :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429934} {:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490374} :activity/id #uuid "76f4a73c-4542-5db3-9e7f-34252998a80c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050308} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490334 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3999a87b-f882-5ca7-9260-d448846a37d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,5,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309187} {:answer/id #uuid "39a5a717-471c-5a17-834f-af512678a057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-13,33,-14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309188} {:answer/id #uuid "7600e36d-9294-520d-95e5-38e4fd4ac988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-12,21,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309669} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc1f13f-1145-50d7-80ea-c9565ed86989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-33,13,-41⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310008} {:answer/id #uuid "fe53bf4d-a431-5742-8703-83bd73a22ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨4,7,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310782}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310008} :answer-field/id #uuid "86549ea0-3e13-5e9e-9d1d-fbd94e79de20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8c5d0e74-0671-5cb7-b3b8-23383905b037" :question/math-academy-id "q-33819" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 23 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $w=⟨4,7,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-33i+13j-41k \\\\  & =⟨-33,13,-41⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-33,13,-41⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "07ae2f09-fe9e-5ba9-a0d7-b2c82c644d07" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490363}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490344 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c55c069-4c02-5970-a366-2d87c0faefc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398349} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c9d880-a1e1-5be5-8507-819f78ea66e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398350} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62040f-08f9-5abf-8ec9-6681c3d75424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398351} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9a749a-2d90-567b-9b9e-9eea1e14d989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbcf038-f3dc-5a71-b0c2-b0f15532c018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} :answer-field/id #uuid "f112cd0f-0678-5784-90d3-7e1ee7077df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2ca5f55d-d481-5b90-9268-9016376d2ff8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490363 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490266 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426d2f86-6e44-5b72-8222-a1d8c826de45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,-5,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489666} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee143c1-2d22-5a6b-8226-53337f0c9aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489742} {:answer/id #uuid "81af70fa-ea19-54cc-83e0-b0a21fab95e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-34,-22,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489809} {:answer/id #uuid "87ba8eac-d335-511b-94ef-29242597cc39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489824} {:answer/id #uuid "a52411c7-786b-5482-9881-e7a8a452b864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨36,22,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf0e22c-7173-584a-ae1b-a7c0bd01e586" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7340caf5-7f57-5ed9-b918-72cd124f498f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70975" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨0,8,-1⟩+t⟨-1,1,7⟩+s⟨3,-5,1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,7⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-5,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =36i+22j+2k \\\\  & =⟨36,22,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨36,22,2⟩.$"} :step/id #uuid "887eff77-49fb-5aec-b491-643d8fc3ea4c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490365}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490365 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11fe6c60-77f7-596d-b73e-0a2b1a46b507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨2,-9,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393066} {:answer/id #uuid "18c27f61-10ac-5e9a-9262-ba682e6d266e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393067} {:answer/id #uuid "a673c983-c8f1-5b15-8abb-116913587299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} {:answer/id #uuid "f377602b-aa7b-52c3-8d62-a25cd478c050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨0,-6,-1⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393069} {:answer/id #uuid "37a16cbe-c7b9-5d98-99c1-895ad8adbfef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨2,-9,0⟩+t⟨3,0,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393068} :answer-field/id #uuid "141932d6-a6f5-58b4-ba12-7fe47a40ab43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "901f1360-df93-5e5e-ac60-c5607de4f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-71036" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(3,6,2),\\,Q(2,-9,0)$, and $R(3,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,-9,0⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-15,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =⟨3,0,1⟩-⟨3,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-6,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨3,6,2⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+s\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+t\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\ r & =⟨3,6,2⟩+s⟨-1,-15,-2⟩+t⟨0,-6,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8eaa6107-75a7-5433-8966-ae16f584399a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490344}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490374 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39cb606-c863-581e-9ff9-2728265a795f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117477} {:answer/id #uuid "54e5a00f-239b-539d-9f9b-5957f11c633b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨6,0,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489715} {:answer/id #uuid "6842561b-d1ec-5753-b48f-a0a96c8d26d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨6,0,2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489762} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea6b719-d65e-5d67-8999-88b13c999f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489776} {:answer/id #uuid "e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490021} :answer-field/id #uuid "54de0330-8cb1-5db4-9316-aaffcc0d2f4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71d2a1f8-b97c-598b-abe7-896238f620c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-32989" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(6,0,2)$ and $B(1,1,3)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,1,3⟩-⟨6,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨6,0,2⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\ r & =⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ab3c66e4-605d-5530-9113-4164fad58316" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490334}}] :activity/title "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489505}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050308 :topic/difficulty 0.8258457054646602 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428372 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction