b-5746-8896-10f0f88087c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128501" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840901d2-388a-56b4-b2ed-4aa835792fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393059} {:answer/id #uuid "3a999e63-69bc-5b5b-ba4a-b3d5b35bdaf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} {:answer/id #uuid "a9567360-7eeb-5790-a68a-54789a38c8f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393061} {:answer/id #uuid "0abc7499-ef02-5049-b4d5-92446ade1dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,20⟩+t⟨0,3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393062} {:answer/id #uuid "d56ba868-cc5e-5eb8-8190-756b44636c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,0,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,7⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393060} :answer-field/id #uuid "74bd7e12-82f3-5b83-88f9-1acb2c12ad74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a1e3ae2d-0bf0-5679-8209-36898e366f4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70981" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c55c069-4c02-5970-a366-2d87c0faefc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,4,1⟩+t⟨5,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398349} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c9d880-a1e1-5be5-8507-819f78ea66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,8,11⟩+s⟨-3,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398350} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62040f-08f9-5abf-8ec9-6681c3d75424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨4,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,5,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398351} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9a749a-2d90-567b-9b9e-9eea1e14d989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} {:answer/id #uuid "3fbcf038-f3dc-5a71-b0c2-b0f15532c018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,5,11⟩+s⟨2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,3,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398352} :answer-field/id #uuid "f112cd0f-0678-5784-90d3-7e1ee7077df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119936 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119649 :question/id #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4942" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b98d4014-27ab-5ffc-a9a1-94f2d76d7cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨3,-9,-5⟩ + t⟨ - 2, 1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117470} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe44dd9-7bdd-5239-bc90-bb3f3d5c8dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117471} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d68798-b39f-5fd9-ad83-ef58d2f0912b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨3,-9,-5⟩ + t⟨ - 5, 0,-2⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117472} {:answer/id #uuid "fd46fa5e-f228-5b17-ab87-937c2c49b057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨6,-8, 0⟩ + t⟨ - 2, 1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117473} {:answer/id #uuid "164382bd-289b-5666-97e1-536a448ecc74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨3, 1, 5⟩ + s⟨6,-8, 0⟩ + t⟨ - 5, 0,-2⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117474}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b6cca1ea-c183-5baf-841b-897aa164800b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a00e2b8e-5c43-5f1e-861a-b8621cd03fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390836} {:answer/id #uuid "d0576584-3750-547a-9169-cba885383592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390837} {:answer/id #uuid "cc58ca2d-f965-5a26-a6a7-4b5c5d9d1c6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390838} {:answer/id #uuid "448cf521-8dea-57c9-a228-ac326b781ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390839} {:answer/id #uuid "e6fdd784-d294-5584-81fc-4a5e521dbe8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390840}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390839} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f59cecd-7538-5379-bf6c-ff75d0435b9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "26d7019c-08c2-5f92-a7e5-2893b8366abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-32988" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(3,1,5),\\,B(6,-8,0)$, and $C(-2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨6,-8,0⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-9,-5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨-2,1,3⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨3,1,5⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39cb606-c863-581e-9ff9-2728265a795f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117477} {:answer/id #uuid "54e5a00f-239b-539d-9f9b-5957f11c633b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨6,0,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489715} {:answer/id #uuid "6842561b-d1ec-5753-b48f-a0a96c8d26d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨6,0,2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489762} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea6b719-d65e-5d67-8999-88b13c999f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489776} {:answer/id #uuid "e994da9e-a986-53ac-b530-86db42005ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490021} :answer-field/id #uuid "54de0330-8cb1-5db4-9316-aaffcc0d2f4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71d2a1f8-b97c-598b-abe7-896238f620c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-32989" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(6,0,2)$ and $B(1,1,3)$, and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,1,3⟩-⟨6,0,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨6,0,2⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\ r & =⟨6,0,2⟩+s⟨3,1,-2⟩+t⟨-5,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09eff712-270d-559e-b2ed-1b87d24b561f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-7,6,-3⟩+t⟨-9,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259965} {:answer/id #uuid "7aaf24c1-4af3-5471-a6e4-7bbde47ce0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260946} {:answer/id #uuid "ac345a14-1f68-5fe2-8828-2ef99a48c407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261380} {:answer/id #uuid "bc74f471-d5ff-5ade-bba5-ec27b6ff5caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨6,3,-7⟩+t⟨-3,9,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261534} {:answer/id #uuid "da3efea4-2fb6-5260-9315-bcfe7be8b9f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨3,7,-6⟩+t⟨-4,3,9⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261802}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260946} :answer-field/id #uuid "859eebf0-098a-5a3c-8e3c-589906da5209" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "016cb0cc-72ee-551e-911e-dc0a1ad297a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128743" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(7,-2,3),\\,V(4,4,-4),$ and $W(3,7,6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{UW},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨4,4,-4⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,-7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨3,7,6⟩-⟨7,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,9,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨7,-2,3⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨-3,6,-7⟩+t⟨-4,9,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03170ce6-1b74-5d0c-a740-266903fa4105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,4,2⟩+t⟨4,-4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259902} {:answer/id #uuid "31b47527-c857-57e6-abe0-41faa15df975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨4,2,6⟩+t⟨-4,-3,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260322} {:answer/id #uuid "3648beed-e103-5bec-8bc9-7ee681a02fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} {:answer/id #uuid "7a29aab3-eefc-5ee1-beae-88249bb83af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,4,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260941} {:answer/id #uuid "a7218829-3284-55b3-b600-8e4433336662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-6,2,4⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260359} :answer-field/id #uuid "0824088c-267c-5eb4-919f-03962a76134c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e20b81af-d8f6-5935-a0ab-531fc6f636f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128760" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262929 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a9595c5-d8f6-5617-b156-92b53851b716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260250} {:answer/id #uuid "5ce9642e-12a2-5cdf-b2c6-8d924f99cc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨2,\\sqrt{5},-3⟩+t⟨4,-2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260672} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdf40e-542c-5dc2-a6fd-921cd50285d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-4,2,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260838} {:answer/id #uuid "98f54aca-662b-5760-8538-8039f017575f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨-3,\\sqrt{5},2⟩+t⟨-4,2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261201} {:answer/id #uuid "c5482cde-9561-5647-92a3-a41687e26ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-5,4,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261615}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260250} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d78a6d-4a26-5561-9d61-b00f371bc511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4a48e326-aaaf-5e46-9d89-fb7681e96383" :question/math-academy-id "q-128761" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(7,-3,4)$ and $Q(5,1,-1),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,1,-1⟩-⟨7,-3,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨7,-3,4⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336bb496-d1df-5e9a-a07a-1ec951355ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302774} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8dad69-2acf-5472-9a3f-505a95ac3fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "b208b020-2e95-5012-90d1-880d0704ce1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303557} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a6125d-748b-50ac-93e6-06be995d0638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303769} {:answer/id #uuid "feb8b07e-b16f-57b2-afdf-a8e6076cfea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308e92-1035-59ed-9244-1f44706e0efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "133e1de3-de48-5298-8948-a57726f1d155" :question/math-academy-id "q-33160" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49c5cfba-30b4-5cd2-bb7b-b9327c517321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨2,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336716} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa30567-9f99-5396-b1b9-f442d2fcaa29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨1,-7,-2⟩+t⟨0,-8,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336976} {:answer/id #uuid "81128713-0ba6-54d5-ad60-664ede84fab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337202} {:answer/id #uuid "8afb07a6-2bd8-5edb-9ec6-22d1e7d02591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337287} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e1912b-7b80-5650-8872-08ddd53cd44c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337202} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6c2ae9-bf70-5d0f-96e8-5aee0a9622bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2d249e59-e724-5332-83de-2d46399e2dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-71034" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $L(-1,-1,1),\\,M(2,5,-3)$, and $N(0,-8,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =⟨2,5,-3⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,6,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =⟨0,-8,-1⟩-⟨-1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $l=⟨-1,-1,1⟩$ of the point $l,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =l+s\\overset{\\to }{LM}+t\\overset{\\to }{LN} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,-1,1⟩+s⟨3,6,-4⟩+t⟨1,-7,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2337c867-1b68-51ab-bed8-d899af940e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336359} {:answer/id #uuid "337484e0-5b6b-5f95-88dc-ef0b3096b39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨3,4,-3⟩+t⟨2,0,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336518} {:answer/id #uuid "38e231b3-4c0e-5717-a0ef-ef6534f1c274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨2,0,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336565} {:answer/id #uuid "4401b429-e065-55ec-a1ab-6464c74d2d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336670} {:answer/id #uuid "f760a7c7-7e6e-53d4-8222-5b484099a2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨3,4,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338201}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336670} :answer-field/id #uuid "489447af-58f8-5125-a63d-1b42d95b0549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "238f448c-c904-543b-b4aa-7c48d6e1e778" :question/math-academy-id "q-71038" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(2,-1,0),\\,V(3,4,-3)$, and $W(2,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{UW},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨3,4,-3⟩-⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{UW} & =⟨2,0,0⟩-⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨2,-1,0⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+s\\overset{\\to }{UV}+t\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\ r & =⟨2,-1,0⟩+s⟨1,5,-3⟩+t⟨0,1,0⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abe04ef1-0077-539a-b85c-52caa98344a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-3,2,4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366207} {:answer/id #uuid "4a96f288-3fd0-537b-806e-046844764150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366208} {:answer/id #uuid "fac45cd4-59c7-516c-bd74-1e4a54e263c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨-3,2,4⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366209} {:answer/id #uuid "4e15b755-6aa5-59e8-8ede-166d794590c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366210} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4ca503-3a78-5aa5-ac98-b7e77b80a651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366211}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186